          "title": "You'll want to know: écraser",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "écraser — \"to crash (as s'écraser); to crush\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Un petit avion s'est écrasé dans la forêt. A small plane crashed in the forest."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Reflexive for a plane that crashes: s'écraser. Without se it is common too, to crush or to mash: écraser des pommes de terre."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "écraser comes from Middle French escraser \"to squash\" (EtymDB), usually traced to a Scandinavian word, Old Norse krasa \"to shatter\"."
            }
          ]
        },
